      <h2>About Nakupenda Sandbank</h2>
      <div>Nakupenda Sandbank is a pristine crescent of white coral sand that emerges from turquoise waters off Stone Town at low tide, accessible by a 20-minute boat ride. The sandbank offers crystal-clear shallow waters perfect for swimming, wading, and snorkeling over healthy coral patches. Day trips typically include a seafood barbecue lunch on the sand, fresh fruit, and snorkeling gear. Best visited at low tide when the sandbank is fully exposed. Combine with Prison Island visit for a perfect half-day excursion.</div>
